# Forgejo Actions runner token — template for nixos/forgejo-runner.sops.env.
# Fill, then: sops -e -i nixos/forgejo-runner.sops.env
# A .sops.env rather than a key in secrets.sops.yaml for the reason spelled out
# in nixos/renovate.sops.env.example.

# Runner registration
# The key MUST be spelled TOKEN: nixpkgs' gitea-actions-runner module wires
# tokenFile straight into EnvironmentFile= and its ExecStartPre reads $TOKEN.
# ONE-SHOT — act_runner trades it for a durable credential in
# /var/lib/gitea-runner/forgejo/.runner and never uses it again; rotating this
# value re-registers nothing unless .runner is gone or the labels changed.
# Until it is filled, ci-secrets.nix writes no runtime file and the unit is
# SKIPPED by ConditionPathExists.
#   Forgejo -> Site Administration -> Actions -> Runners -> Create new runner
#   sopsedit nixos/forgejo-runner.sops.env
#   nixos-rebuild switch --target-host idan@10.0.0.3 --use-remote-sudo --flake .#services-vm
TOKEN=changeme_forgejo_runner_registration_token
